# ---- this fork's build outputs -------------------------------------------
# Everything above is upstream's own ignore list, kept verbatim and in place:
# none of it is removed to make room for the entries below, and none of it
# swallows a file this fork adds. `build/` matches a directory named build, not
# the build.zig file at the root or consumer/build.zig.
#
# `.zig-cache/` and `zig-out/` are directories rather than single files because
# a normal user build creates both, and a normal user build must not dirty the
# tree or leak into a package published from it.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own output
# tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so that a build
# run from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/

# Nix and development-environment outputs. `package.nix`, `flake.nix`,
# `devenv.nix`, `devenv.yaml` and `.envrc` are tracked; what those files
# *produce* is not. `nix build` writes a `result` symlink beside the flake
# (and `result-<name>` for a named output), `devenv` keeps its loaded state in
# `.devenv/`, and `direnv` — which `.envrc` exists for — keeps its cache in
# `.direnv/`. None of these three patterns can swallow a file this fork ships:
# no shipped path is named `result` or starts with `.devenv`/`.direnv`.
result
result-*
.devenv/
.direnv/
